```powershell
# From: e:\APPS\Sonique\

# Compile only (fast check):
./gradlew :composeApp:compileDebugKotlinAndroid

# Full debug APK:
./gradlew :composeApp:assembleDebug

# Clean build:
./gradlew clean :composeApp:assembleDebug
```
> Note: Config cache is frequently invalidated. Expected warnings about deprecated AGP options —
> these are pre-existing and NOT caused by our changes. Focus on `e:` errors only.
> **Do NOT build unless the user explicitly asks.** The user builds from Android Studio.


## 7. Conventions & Rules
1. **Always use `CRLF` line endings** — Windows project, files use `\r\n`
2. **KMP-first**: Any new logic goes in `commonMain` unless it is platform-specific (camera, BackHandler, etc.)
3. **No hardcoded strings** — use `Res.string.*` from `composeResources/values/strings.xml`
4. **Imports matter**: Missing imports are a common build failure cause.
   - `ArtistEntity` → `com.sonique.domain.data.entities.ArtistEntity`
   - `SongEntity` → `com.sonique.domain.data.entities.SongEntity`
   - `LocalResource` → `com.sonique.domain.utils.LocalResource`
   - `BackHandler` → `com.sonique.app.expect.ui.BackHandler`
   - `LibraryChipType` → `com.sonique.common.LibraryChipType`
   - `MERGING_DATA_TYPE` → `com.sonique.common.MERGING_DATA_TYPE`
   - `Track` → `com.sonique.domain.data.model.browse.album.Track`
   - `GenericMediaItem` → `com.sonique.domain.data.player.GenericMediaItem`
   - `NowPlayingTrackState` → `com.sonique.domain.mediaservice.handler.NowPlayingTrackState`
   - `DataStoreManager` → `com.sonique.domain.manager.DataStoreManager`
5. **Null safety**: Prefer `data?.isNotEmpty() == true` over `!data.isNullOrEmpty()` to avoid
   compiler issues with nullable `StateFlow` data
6. **Do NOT touch `SharedViewModel`** unless explicitly asked — it is large (~62KB) and complex
7. **Do NOT build** unless the user explicitly says to build. The user builds from Android Studio.
8. **Verify build** after significant changes: always run `compileDebugKotlinAndroid` before claiming done
   (only when the user asks you to verify)


## 8. Common Pitfalls (Lessons Learned)
- **Extra braces**: When editing `LibraryItem.kt`, the `if-else if` chain for `LibraryItemType`
  variants is fragile — always verify brace counts after edits
- **`@Composable` context**: Ensure `LazyRow { items(...) }` blocks are inside a `@Composable` scope
- **`BackHandler` expect/actual**: The expect is in `commonMain/expect/ui/`, actual is in `androidMain/expect/ui/`
- **ArtistEntity import in LibraryScreen**: Must be imported explicitly even if the type is only
  used transitively (Kotlin strict mode)
- The `CanvasSong` block in `LibraryItem.kt` uses `item.canvasThumbUrl` — `item` must be cast to
  `SongEntity` first via `val song = item as? SongEntity ?: return@items`
- **NowPlayingTrackState stale data**: When a new song starts, the first emission has the new
  `mediaItem`/`track` but the OLD `songEntity`. Always check `songEntity.videoId == videoId` before
  using songEntity data. Use `distinctUntilChangedBy { Pair(it.mediaItem.mediaId, it.songEntity?.videoId) }`
  to receive both the initial and database-resolved updates.
- **Track.thumbnails is `List<Thumbnail>?`**, not a `String`. To get the URL, use
  `track.thumbnails?.lastOrNull()?.url`. SongEntity.thumbnails IS a `String?`.
- **SongEntity.artistName is `List<String>?`**, not a `String`. Use `.joinToString(", ")` to display.
- **DataStore preferences**: All boolean-like prefs use `TRUE`/`FALSE` string constants, not actual booleans.
  Flows return `Flow<String>`, not `Flow<Boolean>`. Compare with `== DataStoreManager.TRUE`.
- **ModalBottomSheet.kt** is ~137KB — be very careful with edits. Prefer targeted line-range edits.
- **NowPlayingScreen.kt** is ~108KB — same caution applies.


## 9. Recent Features & Session History
- Implemented Material 3 Expressive player controls (squircle play/pause, pill skip buttons,
  outlined shuffle/repeat, animated wavy seekbar track with pill thumb) — togglable from Settings > Appearance
- Added `rubberyClick` modifier with dual-spring zoom/bounce animation for player control buttons
  (press: stiff spring to 0.86x, release: under-damped spring with overshoot bounce)
- Replaced all pure-white player UI elements with cream-white `Color(0xFFFAF9F6)` for premium feel
- Fixed NowPlayingTrackState stale-data bug where old song metadata showed on track change
- Synced MiniPlayer to use `nowPlayingScreenData` for consistent metadata display
- One-time migration to force-disable "Frosted Player Background" on update (`frosted_force_disabled_v4`)
- Changed default for `BLUR_PLAYER_BACKGROUND` from `TRUE` to `FALSE`
- Implemented `LibraryChipType` back navigation with granular `BackHandler`
- Added "Followed Artists" section to Library dashboard with `LazyRow` of circular items
- Liked Music was removed from the library dashboard (user's request)


